From cac83ac7689cb1b62d8242b498ea7c0307ee2b19 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jared Wyles <jared.wyles@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 21:00:00 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 17/32] skippy: restore resident prefixes as shared cells plus
 recurrent checkpoints

The move to the new llama.cpp pin rebuilt the native queue from an older
snapshot and lost the resident-prefix module the Rust side is built against:
skippy_session_export_resident_kv_page,
skippy_session_export_resident_recurrent_state and
skippy_session_resident_prefix_bytes no longer existed, so a runtime built
from the queue failed to load, and hybrid and recurrent models lost resident
prefixes altogether.

This brings src/skippy/resident_prefix.cpp back as James Dumay left it on
the previous pin. A saved prefix keeps its attention cells in the shared pool under a
cache-owned sequence id; only the fixed-size recurrent state is copied, into
a checkpoint the cache owns, serialized with upstream's host writer
(llama_io_write_host_create). Restores share the retained cells and rebuild a
private recurrent row. The save, restore, create-from-prefix, drop, used
cells and recurrent export/import entry points move back from state.cpp, and
the model again keeps checkpoints per cache sequence rather than one token
list per lane.

The memory cache capabilities report SKIPPY_MEMORY_CACHE_RESIDENT_ATTENTION
and SKIPPY_MEMORY_CACHE_RESIDENT_CHECKPOINT again, recurrent and hybrid
memories advertise resident prefixes, and a non-unified context advertises
none. A model opens with a unified pool even with one lane, so cache-owned
sequence ids share it.

skippy-sampling-history regains its resident mode, the long GPU checkpoint
proof and the host-writer regression, merged with the verify-window and
exact-checkpoint cases the new pin added.

ABI inventory (backward compatibility with older runtimes is not kept; the
Rust mirror changes in lockstep):
- added: skippy_session_export_resident_kv_page,
  skippy_session_export_resident_recurrent_state,
  skippy_session_resident_prefix_bytes (include/skippy/state.h,
  src/skippy/resident_prefix.cpp)
- added: SKIPPY_MEMORY_CACHE_RESIDENT_CHECKPOINT (1 << 3),
  SKIPPY_MEMORY_CACHE_RESIDENT_ATTENTION (1 << 4)
- removed: none

Bumps the Skippy ABI from 0.1.70 to 0.1.71; the model-support lane's bumps
follow from there.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QA3dWey3RBtBgDz1Tery9Y
